Chapter: TypeClassPoly

 A class with a superclass carries the superclass's dictionary.

 synth-class-type-defs gives SortableDict a field __super-Equatable of type
 EquatableDict. Nothing used to put a value in it: the instance dictionary was
 built from the instance's own methods alone, so the field was left to __alloc,
 which zero-fills. Every superclass dictionary of every instance of every class
 that had one was a null pointer.

 It stayed invisible because the two halves of the bug cancelled. The PARSE
 keep-deck copy dropped ClassDef.superclass on the floor, so the desugarer saw
 no superclass, never added the field to the record, and never missed it.
 Repairing the copy left the field present and empty.

 This chapter used to name Equatable as a superclass without declaring it
 anywhere, and the dangling reference resolved to nothing and bothered no one
 -- which is what an erased constraint buys you. Equatable is declared here
 now, with an instance for Integer, so the constraint is real.

class Equatable where
  equals : a, a -> Boolean

instance Equatable Integer where
  equals (x) (y) = x == y

class Converter where
  convert : a, b -> b

instance Converter Integer where
  convert (x) (y) = y

class Equatable a => Sortable where
  sort-key : a -> Integer

instance Sortable Integer where
  sort-key (x) = x

Section: Helpers

  test-convert : Text
  test-convert = show (convert 1 42)

  test-sort-key : Text
  test-sort-key = show (sort-key 5)

 Reach through the Sortable dictionary into the superclass dictionary it now
 carries, and call the superclass method out of it. A zeroed __super-Equatable
 is a null pointer, and this is the line that finds out.

  test-super : Text
  test-super =
   let d = Sortable-dict-Integer
   in let eq = d.__super-Equatable
   in show ((eq.equals-impl) 7 7)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni test-convert
    print-line-uni test-sort-key
    print-line-uni test-super
  end
